  [gate 23i] --no-datapath-probes planted in a throwaway config reached the build.sh arty launch line at position 6 of 34 with build.sh unedited; the other 26 design tokens and the 5-token flow tail are the unplanted line's, verbatim
test_toolchain_patches_are_applied:
  [gate 23h] the 5 patches in sw/litex/patches are the 5 apply.sh applies, and reversing them off this interpreter's trees and re-applying them reproduces all 4 installed files byte for byte, including 1 that two patches share and must therefore compose on ({'gmii.py': ['0002-liteeth-gmii-tx-clk-invert.patch', '0007-liteeth-gmii-rx-capture.patch']}). Upstream LiteX has no `baremetal` VexiiRiscv variant and the revision it pins rejects the --l2-* arguments four configs pass, so this is what lets gates 23f/23g elaborate at all. It says nothing about whether the patches are CORRECT, only that the tree is the one described here
test_front_end_routing_per_board:
  [gate 24c] per-board front-end routing: tdm routed {'arty': True, 'ax7101': True}; 3 configs checked at BOTH tdm_bus_wired() states; the refusal runs before the platform is built; o_i2s_mclk_o binds only to i2s_pads[0] (pmoda:4 D13) or tdm_pads
